{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"Toolport.Toolport","latestVersion":"2.3.4","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) Brandon South","description":"Local-first MCP gateway. One port for every tool and every AI client.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"README","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport#readme"}],"license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) Brandon South","description":"Local-first MCP gateway. One port for every tool and every AI client.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"README","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport#readme"}],"license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Toolport is a local gateway that aggregates every MCP server on your machine and\nshares them with every AI client you use, so a server is configured once rather\nthan once per client.\n\nIn lazy mode, Toolport exposes a small MCP tool catalog and discovers full tool\ndefinitions on demand, which cuts context for clients that otherwise load every\ntool definition. Servers, credentials, and access sets are managed in one app:\nsecrets live in the OS keychain, tool definitions are pinned and re-checked so a\nchanged tool is flagged (and quarantined in Strict mode), and destructive calls\ncan require human approval.\n\nRuns entirely on your machine. There is no account, and no tool traffic leaves the\ndevice unless a server you configured sends it.","moniker":"toolport","name":"Toolport","packageUrl":"https://toolport.app","publisher":"Toolport","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/issues","publisherUrl":"https://toolport.app","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/releases/tag/v2.3.4","tags":["agent","ai","claude","cli","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gateway","llm","local-first","mcp","model-context-protocol"]}},"longDescription":"Toolport is a local gateway that aggregates every MCP server on your machine and\nshares them with every AI client you use, so a server is configured once rather\nthan once per client.\n\nIn lazy mode, Toolport exposes a small MCP tool catalog and discovers full tool\ndefinitions on demand, which cuts context for clients that otherwise load every\ntool definition. Servers, credentials, and access sets are managed in one app:\nsecrets live in the OS keychain, tool definitions are pinned and re-checked so a\nchanged tool is flagged (and quarantined in Strict mode), and destructive calls\ncan require human approval.\n\nRuns entirely on your machine. There is no account, and no tool traffic leaves the\ndevice unless a server you configured sends it.","moniker":"toolport","name":"Toolport","packageUrl":"https://toolport.app","publisher":"Toolport","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/issues","publisherUrl":"https://toolport.app","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/btsouth/toolport/releases/tag/v2.3.4","tags":["agent","ai","claude","cli","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gateway","llm","local-first","mcp","model-context-protocol"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.3.4/app.json","detailSha256":"bd1f38b11aa3e2ab23dc68a88371732156bc4bc4e87da27041f48769046e152d","releaseDate":"2026-11-09","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"2.3.4"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.3.3/app.json","detailSha256":"f493d65ba032dac40abac2e670bf72a596e67e98f50333fe66105f24cb0df47e","releaseDate":"2026-11-04","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.3.3"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.3.2/app.json","detailSha256":"a9860edc997b9833a1d12106aa01cb4144e13018a11223189f4b1ca3a0131c7c","releaseDate":"2026-11-03","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.3.2"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.3.1/app.json","detailSha256":"97f